"distinct_partners\": 4, \"events\": 4, \"node\": 1877}, {\"distinct_partners\": 16, \"events\": 16, \"node\": 1932}], \"window\": [4302, 42701]}", "latency_ms": 11, "tokens_before": 18903, "tokens_after": 18903, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_2025d7ec", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [798, 131, 389, 45, 972, 1877, 1932], "window": [4302, 42701], "confidence": 0.66, "narrative": "798 sends only to {45,389} while 131 receives only from {972,1877,1932} \u2014 disjoint sets requiring a 3+ hop relay. The static 389-131 edge points 131->389, so the hub cannot deliver into 131. 798 emits just 4 events over 38k time units, isolated in separate temporal bins with four empty bins between them, and the required terminal relays (972, 1877 with 4 events each) are near-silent. In a graph averaging ~0.13 events/time unit, chaining 3+ hops with every gap under 600 units is not supported. The apparent 798-131 link is an artifact of hub 389 (151 partners) once time is ignored, plus 131's late-window popularity \u2014 both explicitly insufficient.", "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structural bottleneck (directional):**\n- 798's out-neighbors: only **{45, 389}** (step_04)\n- 131's in-neighbors: only **{972, 1877, 1932}** (step_05)\n\nThese sets are disjoint, so any influence path needs **\u22653 hops**. Notably, step_02 shows a static 389\u2013131 edge, but step_05 proves it runs *131\u2192389*, not 389\u2192131 \u2014 so the hub gives no direct delivery into 131.\n\n**Confounder control \u2014 the hub illusion:** Node 389 has 151 distinct partners / 170 events (step_08). It is what makes 798 and 131 look \"connected\" when time is ignored (step_02). That is precisely the insufficient evidence the task warns about.\n\n**Temporal feasibility fails:** 798 emits only **4 events across 38,399 time units** (step_03), and they are scattered into separate bins \u2014 2 in [9102,13901], 1 in [23502,28301], 1 in [33102,37901], with four empty bins (step_06). The whole graph averages ~0.13 events/time unit (step_01, 4954 events). A 600-unit relay budget per hop is a tiny slice of this timeline, and the required terminal relays are themselves near-silent: 972 and 1877 have just 4 events each, 1932 has 16 (step_08). 131's own traffic peaks in [23502,28301] (step_07), which is *late* activity \u2014 recent popularity, not a hand-off traceable to 798.\n\n**Conclusion:** No time-respecting chain with \u2264600-unit gaps can plausibly bridge 798's four isolated emissions to 131's three sparse in-neighbors. The apparent connection is a static hub artifact.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_2025d7ec\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [798, 131, 389, 45, 972, 1877, 1932],\n  \"window\": [4302, 42701],\n  \"confidence\": 0.66,\n  \"narrative\": \"798 sends only to {45,389} while 131 receives only from {972,1877,1932} \u2014 disjoint sets requiring a 3+ hop relay. The static 389-131 edge points 131->389, so the hub cannot deliver into 131. 798 emits just 4 events over 38k time units, isolated in separate temporal bins with four empty bins between them, and the required terminal relays (972, 1877 with 4 events each) are near-silent. In a graph averaging ~0.13 events/time unit, chaining 3+ hops with every gap under 600 units is not supported. The apparent 798-131 link is an artifact of hub 389 (151 partners) once time is ignored, plus 131's late-window popularity \u2014 both explicitly insufficient.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 25283, "total_output_tokens": 5816, "total_tokens": 31099, "total_latency_ms": 83377, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}